stories.summary:
It's that time ladies and gents.... time to go on the record with some bold predictions for 2026!



	 



	2025 was a case of near misses for my bolds. I had three miss by a whisker:



	- Falcons to lead the league in sacks (they were second behind only the Broncos);



	- Allen to set a career high in completion % and go over 70% (he set a career high but ended with 69.3% regular season);



	- Matt Milano to break his career best of 3.5 sacks (he matched his previous high and lodged 3.5 sacks for a second time).



	 



	So with just a little more luck let's hope to land some this year. As ever I will do 4 NFL wide and 4 Bills specific:



	 



	Rest of NFL



	- New Orleans Saints to win the NFC South and host the NFC Championship game;



	- Green Bay Packers to finish 8-9, miss the playoffs, and fire Matt LaFleur;



	- five of the seven AFC Playoff teams to be different in 2026 to those that qualified in 2025;



	- Cam Ward to throw for over 4,000 yards and at least 30 touchdowns



	 



	Bills



	- DJ Moore to lead the Bills in yards, but not in receptions or touchdowns;



	- Greg Rousseau to post double digit sacks and be voted as a second team all-pro;



	- Rookie 4th round pick Kaleb Elams-Orr to lead the Bills in snaps among interior linebackers;



	- Buffalo to come out of the Kansas City game on Thanksgiving below .500, then run the table and make the playoffs. 



	 



	 



	As ever, flame away and add your own!
